# Telegram Bot API reverse proxy for rawrter-tg-bot. Runs on the Frankfurt box (2.26.108.249).
#
# Why: prod lives in RF, where api.telegram.org is cut by SNI-based DPI — raw TCP to a foreign
# host passes, a TLS handshake with SNI api.telegram.org does not. The bot talks to
# https://tg.rawrter.com instead (TELEGRAM_API_BASE_URL in /opt/rawrter-tg-bot/.env); this Caddy
# terminates TLS and re-originates to api.telegram.org from outside RF.
#
# Prereq: A record tg.rawrter.com -> 2.26.108.249 (Caddy needs it for the Let's Encrypt cert).
# Only the prod boxes may use it: everyone else gets the connection dropped. The bot token is in
# the URL path, so no access log is configured — Caddy logs no requests by default.
{
	email nusferatus64@gmail.com
}

tg.rawrter.com {
	# 89.191.225.228 = prod (AdminVPS, Moscow); 201.51.6.246 = old prod, until it is retired.
	@prod remote_ip 89.191.225.228 201.51.6.246
	handle @prod {
		reverse_proxy https://api.telegram.org {
			header_up Host api.telegram.org
		}
	}
	handle {
		abort
	}
}
